  <user_flow>
    <primary_path><![CDATA[
**Step 1: Load auth screen**
- User arrives from landing or deep link
- Form title indicates mode (Login or Register)
- Email input focused, password hidden

**Step 2: Enter credentials**
- User types email → validation on blur
- User types password → strength meter appears (registration mode)
- Optional: Show "Forgot password?" link if login mode

**Step 3: Submit form**
- Click "Continue" → validation runs
- If valid: POST /auth/login or /auth/register
- Button morphs to loading state (pill shape, spinner)

**Step 4: Success or error**
- Success: Redirect to dashboard or onboarding
- Error: Show inline error banner, preserve form state
- User can retry or switch to OAuth

**Step 5: OAuth alternative**
- Click "Google" or "Apple" button
- Redirect to OAuth provider consent screen
- After consent: redirect to dashboard

**Step 6: Form toggle**
- User clicks "Don't have an account? Sign up"
- Form title and button text update
- Email field preserved, password cleared
- Validation rules switch to registration mode
    ]]></primary_path>

    <edge_cases><![CDATA[
**Account already exists (registration mode):**
- Email validation returns error "Account already exists"
- Show suggestion to "Log in instead" with toggle link

**Invalid email format:**
- Email validation runs on blur
- Show error "Please enter a valid email address"
- Error clears when user corrects input

**Weak password (registration):**
- Password strength meter shows red
- Submit button disabled if password too weak
- Error message explains requirements

**Server error:**
- Show MEGAPHONE error banner: "Sign-in failed. Please try again."
- CTAs remain functional
- Log error to Sentry

**Slow network:**
- Button shows loading state immediately on click
- Prevent double-submission (button disabled during request)
- Show timeout error after 10s

**OAuth consent denied:**
- User cancels OAuth screen
- Return to auth form
- Show warning banner "You canceled sign-in. Please try again."
    ]]></edge_cases>
  </user_flow>

  <states>
    <default><![CDATA[
- Auth form visible with email focused
- Password input masked
- Submit button enabled
- OAuth buttons enabled
- No error banners
    ]]></default>

    <loading><![CDATA[
- Submit button morphs to pill shape (blockRiot03 → pillMarch01)
- Button shows spinner overlay
- Button disabled (opacity 0.6)
- All other inputs disabled
- OAuth buttons disabled
    ]]></loading>

    <error><![CDATA[
- MEGAPHONE error banner above form: "Sign-in failed" or specific error
- Affected field highlights in red (e.g., email field if account not found)
- Error message appears below field
- Submit button re-enabled for retry
- Form state preserved
    ]]></error>

    <success><![CDATA[
- Form briefly shows success state (1-2 seconds)
- Success banner appears: "Signed in successfully"
- Navigation happens automatically to /dashboard or onboarding
    ]]></success>
  </states>

